Hi Nick,
Thank you for your kind help! I think my reply to your suggestions got lost somewhere. Here's the reply again. I successfully installed some rexpokit binaries in R but after calling the package I got an installation error suggesting rexpokit was installed in a previous version of R. I then tried to re-install rexpokit (and all my packages) to my newest R version  (RStudio 2023.09.1+494 "Desert Sunflower" Release for macOS) following the re-installation code below, which in turn, removed rexpokit from my library. What do you think could be happening? I appreciate your and everyone's guidance on this matter.

Installation error
> library(rexpokit)
Error: package or namespace load failed for ‘rexpokit’:
 package ‘rexpokit’ was installed before R 4.0.0: please re-install it

Re-installation code
# check your package library path
.libPaths()

# grab old packages names
old_packages <- installed.packages(lib.loc = "/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/4.3-x86_64/Resources/library")
old_packages <- as.data.frame(old_packages)
list.of.packages <- unlist(old_packages$Package)

# remove old packages
remove.packages(installed.packages( priority = "NA" )[,1] )

# reinstall all packages
new.packages <- list.of.packages[!(list.of.packages %in% installed.packages()[,"Package"])]
if(length(new.packages)) install.packages(new.packages)
lapply(list.of.packages,function(x){library(x,character.only=TRUE)})

Working binaries

